"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The showcase builder therefore emits properties, task records, attachment metadata, review state, tags, and named version checkpoints alongside pages. The restore verification compares table contents and file hashes after a complete round trip."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stable references"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This package assigns deterministic UUIDs to pages and assets from source keys. Cross-page links and excerpt references resolve through those IDs. Keep a page's source key when changing its title. Renaming a key creates a new identity; it is a content migration, not a cosmetic edit."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The custom macro directives in the source Markdown contain real editor nodes. They are removed during conversion and become editable native blocks in Kollab. Unsupported node names or unresolved "},{"type":"text","text":"page:","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" references fail the build."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Source: examples/kollab-team/pages/document-model.md"}]}]}

{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"macroBlock","attrs":{"type":"page-properties","config":{"properties":[{"key":"Area","value":"Engineering","type":"text"},{"key":"Audience","value":"Developers and operators","type":"text"},{"key":"Availability","value":"Reference; see section status","type":"text"}]}}},{"type":"calloutPanel","attrs":{"type":"note","title":"Design reference"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This page follows the repository design document. Some sections retain proposed or historical behavior. Check the curated Architecture walkthrough and current source code before treating a planned capability as available."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This document details the architecture, configurations, and collaborative sync loop of the Tiptap/ProseMirror editor canvas in Project Kollab, as well as read-only editing states and document statistics."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Local development endpoint"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Vite development server is configured for "},{"type":"text","text":"http://localhost:8090","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"text","text":"strictPort: true","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":". The Go server's local authentication configuration, CORS allowlist, Docker development environment, and Playwright base URL use the same browser origin. The API and WebSocket proxy use host port "},{"type":"text","text":"8081","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; the Go service continues to listen on port "},{"type":"text","text":"8080","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" inside Docker."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"dev.sh","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the repository launcher for this composition. It first probes the active Docker context with "},{"type":"text","text":"docker info","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":". If the daemon is unavailable and the "},{"type":"text","text":"colima","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" executable exists, the launcher synchronously runs "},{"type":"text","text":"colima start","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; otherwise, it exits with instructions to start Docker. It then resolves the supported Docker Compose command, runs "},{"type":"text","text":"docker-compose.dev.yml","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in detached mode, installs frontend dependencies only when absent, and uses "},{"type":"text","text":"exec npm run dev","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" so the terminal is attached to Vite. "},{"type":"text","text":"dev.sh --down","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" delegates cleanup to Docker Compose; interrupting Vite does not stop the development containers."}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. Tiptap & ProseMirror Core Architecture"}]},{"type":"calloutPanel","attrs":{"type":"note","title":"NOTE"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Status:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 🟢 Completed"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Kollab utilizes a headless editor model where the DOM is managed React-declaratively, while the underlying document model is tracked as a ProseMirror Abstract Syntax Tree (AST)."}]},{"type":"macroBlock","attrs":{"type":"mermaid","config":{"code":"---
